            <ArticleTitle>Intrabronchial lesion due to Cladosporium sphaerospermum in a healthy, non-asthmatic woman.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>348-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An intrabronchial lesion caused by to Cladosporium sphaerospermum in a healthy and non-asthmatic 59-year-old woman is reported. Intrabronchial infusion of amphotericin B was repeated three times followed by oral administration of prednisolone and itraconazole. The findings on chest radiographs subsequently improved. The possibility of intrabronchial lesions caused by C. sphaerosporum even in a healthy and non-asthmatic person is remarkable.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
